abstract: >
  PrimeCounter Pro is a high-performance prime counting function π(N) 
  implementation that achieves sub-second queries up to 10^16 using 
  only 9.2 MB of precomputed data. It combines segmented sieving, 
  bidirectional optimization, and JIT compilation to deliver 
  performance comparable to specialized algorithms like Meissel-Lehmer, 
  while maintaining extreme simplicity and minimal memory footprint.
